\ Dogfood: Slice 5 fixed-size arrays + usize, Slice 6 references, and Phase 4
\ Slice 1's multi-output ABI. A bounded `i64` stack over an embedded array
\ and a runtime `usize` cursor, exercising array-as-field, the runtime
\ cursor (the bounds-trap path), in-place mutation through `&!>`, a
\ non-consuming read through `&>`/`@`, and `len`.
\
\ `pop`/`peek` return their two results (the updated `Stack` and the read
\ value) directly as `( Stack -- Stack i64 )`: a user-defined word may now
\ return more than one value through a call (the multi-output aggregate-
\ return ABI), so no hand-written bundle struct is needed.

import: intrinsics * ;

type: Stack 
  items array[i64 16] 
  top usize ;

: empty ( -- Stack )
  0 16 fill 0 >usize Stack ;

: push ( Stack i64 -- Stack )
  | s x |
  &s &top @ | i |
  &!s &!items i &!> x !   \ write in place, no whole-array rebuild
  &s &top @ 1 add | newtop |
  s &!top newtop ! ;

: pop ( Stack -- Stack i64 )
  | s |
  &s &top @ 1 sub | i |
  &s &items i &> @ | v |  \ read without aliasing the array
  s &!top i ! v ;

: peek ( Stack -- Stack i64 )
  | s |
  &s &top @ 1 sub | i |
  &s &items i &> @ | v |
  s v ;

: main ( -- )
  empty
  1 push 2 push 3 push
  peek .                        \ 3, non-consuming: stack unchanged underneath
  pop .                         \ 3
  pop .                         \ 2
  peek .                        \ 1, one item left
  &items @ swap drop
  len .                         \ 16, len is a compile-time constant of the array shape
  drop ;                        \ discard the residual items array
